Topic: Arrays Level 2 (Important Patterns)

⏱️ ~45 minutes

1️⃣ Pattern 1: Second Largest Element 🔥 (VERY COMMON)
Approach:
Track largest & second largest
arr = [10, 50, 20, 80, 30]

first = second = float('-inf')

for num in arr:
    if num > first:
        second = first
        first = num
    elif num > second and num != first:
        second = num

print("Second Largest:", second)
2️⃣ Pattern 2: Check if Array is Sorted
arr = [1, 2, 3, 4]

is_sorted = True

for i in range(len(arr) - 1):
    if arr[i] > arr[i + 1]:
        is_sorted = False
        break

print(is_sorted)
3️⃣ Pattern 3: Move Zeros to End 🔥

👉 Important interview question

arr = [0, 1, 0, 3, 12]

pos = 0

for i in range(len(arr)):
    if arr[i] != 0:
        arr[pos], arr[i] = arr[i], arr[pos]
        pos += 1

print(arr)
4️⃣ Pattern 4: Remove Duplicates (Sorted Array)
arr = [1, 1, 2, 2, 3]

unique = []

for num in arr:
    if num not in unique:
        unique.append(num)

print(unique)
🧠 Interview Tricks
Use two pointers (left/right)
Avoid extra space if possible
Think in patterns, not questions
